ils in week 6 is visible in week 1; a lost run restarts from the start of any earlier week.","intent":"COMBINE — One Loud Night. Aha: Last Call is a warning, not the end: a ring must stay full for TWO weeks in a row to end the run. The night market M up the hill triples in week 3 and its ring is forecast to hit Last Call that week, so the carriage looks like it belongs on the market line M-h-A. But the market's queue drains the week after, while the street line A-B-C-D-E (4 hops, 27 seats) is short of seats EVERY week and its rings creep up until they stay full. Put the carriage on the street line and let the market ring flash once: the forecast shows it full in week 3 only, then falling. Why: Combines the market day with carriages and the city's calm-overcrowding rule, read straight off the forecast: a one-week spike is survivable, a slow leak is not. Proof (intended plan, replayed): 242 delivered, goal 220, 3 stars. Trap: the carriage on the market line M-h-A, because its ring is forecast to hit Last Call in week 3 — loses: M full wk4.","mechanics":["carriages","hills","market day"],"optimal":8,"branching":5,"trap":0,"explored":3596},{"n":83,"grid":"A-B-C\n|   |\nD   |\n|   |\nF   E\n    |\n    I\nstations: A leaf → 6 drop, 1 moon, 1 kite; B drop → 6 leaf, 2 kite; C kite → 2 drop, 2 lantern; D moon (market wk3) → 1 leaf, 2 kite; F key → 1 moon, 1 leaf; E star → 2 kite, 2 lantern; I lantern (market wk5) → 4 leaf, 3 kite, 2 star\n7 weeks · tracks wk1 +6 · 2 lines · cards wk2: calm: halve every queue | +1 carriage · goal 203 of 290 riders · 3rd star: no station reaches amber","legend":"MAP: capital letters = stations (glyph + weekly demand listed under the map); - | \\ / x = rail corridors a line may use (x = two diagonals crossing). TRACKS vs HOPS: one corridor between two stations costs ONE track however long it is drawn ('A---B' is 1 track), but its HOPS are its length in station spacings ('A-B' 1 hop, 'A---B' 2 hops) and each h on it adds 1 more hop; a line's hop