l wk5.","mechanics":["heritage stations"],"optimal":5,"branching":5,"trap":0,"explored":380},{"n":110,"grid":"A-B-C\n|    \\\nD     E\n|    /\nG---F\nstations: A leaf (HERITAGE) → 6 drop, 4 kite; B drop → 4 star, 3 leaf; C star → 4 drop, 3 moon; D kite → 4 leaf, 3 star; E moon (HERITAGE) → 1 leaf, 1 lantern; G lantern → 4 kite, 3 key; F key → 4 moon, 3 kite\n6 weeks · tracks wk1 +8 · 2 lines · loops allowed · goal 257 of 282 riders · 3rd star: finish with 2 tracks to spare","legend":"MAP: capital letters = stations (glyph + weekly demand listed under the map); - | \\ / x = rail corridors a line may use (x = two diagonals crossing). TRACKS vs HOPS: one corridor between two stations costs ONE track however long it is drawn ('A---B' is 1 track), but its HOPS are its length in station spacings ('A-B' 1 hop, 'A---B' 2 hops) and each h on it adds 1 more hop; a line's hops set its seats. ~ = river crossing (needs a tunnel); h = hill (each h adds 1 hop: slower trains); = = ferry over deep water (+1 hop, a ferry carries at most 12 riders a week per carriage set); > < v ^ = one-way rail (a line using it only runs once closed into a loop that follows the arrows); . empty ground; , water. RULES: a line is one path along corridors (extend only from its two ends); passengers ride to the nearest station showing the glyph they want (nearest = fewest line changes, then fewest hops, along the lines drawn; the in-game route preview shows it), changing lines at any shared station. A station with no demand listed sends nobody (its card shows 0 riders). Station rows read 'A leaf → 2 star, 1 drop' = A shows a Leaf and sends 2 riders a week who want a Star and 1 who wants a Drop. A line's weekly seats = 6 x (1 + carriages) x 36 / (2 x its hops) — short lines run often; loops count hops once (twice as often). Each week riders appear, ride, queue if no seat; a station holding 12 (24 at an interchange #) is full: 'Last Call'; full 2 weeks in a row ends the run (heritage ! stations may never be full). Win = reach the last week having delivered the goal. Week events: stations marked @w open in week w (visible from the start), *w = market day (3x demand that week), snow weeks halve every train's seats, rush weeks multiply demand. MOVES: new line, extend a line end, close a loop, add carriage, interchange upgrade, pick the weekly card, undo this week's edits, run the week. PLANNING AIDS: while planning, every ring shows its FORECAST (how full it gets by the last week if the network stays as drawn) and the HUD shows projected deliveries vs the goal, so a week-1 plan that fails in week 6 is visible in week 1; a lost run restarts from the start of any earlier week.","intent":"PRACTISE — Two Old Gates. Aha: Two heritage gates, but read their demand cards: the west gate A sends 10 riders a week to its neighbours B and D, the east gate E only 2. The ring looks like Ringvale's loop puzzle, yet one 8-hop loop (27 seats for 47 riders) lets the busy gate A fill by week 3. Break the ring instead and give A a short line among its own riders, G-D-A-B, with B-C-E-F for the rest: the quiet gate E is safe on the longer line, and two tracks stay spare. Why: Practise: the heritage rule where the two gates are NOT alike. Proof (intended plan, replayed): 282 delivered, goal 257, 3 stars. Trap: the Ringvale habit: close the whole ring A-B-C-E-F-G-D (8 hops, 27 seats), and the busy gate A fills in week 3 — loses: A,B,C,D,G,F full wk3.","mechanics":["loop lines","heritage stations"],"optimal":7,"branching":7,"trap":0,"explored":4263},{"n":111,"grid":"  H\n / \\\nA   B\n|   |\nC-E-D\nstations: H moon (HERITAGE) → 5 kite, 5 drop; A leaf → 5 kite, 3 moon; B star → 5 drop, 3 moon; C kite → 5 leaf, 3 star; E lantern → 3 moon, 3 kite, 3 drop; D drop → 5 star, 3 leaf\n6 weeks · tracks wk1 +6 · 2 lines · rush wk4 x1.25, wk5 x1.5 · loops allowed · goal 302 of 351 riders · 3rd star: no station reaches amber","legend":"MAP: capital letters = stations (glyph + weekly demand listed under the 