 in a row ends the run (heritage ! stations may never be full). Win = reach the last week having delivered the goal. Week events: stations marked @w open in week w (visible from the start), *w = market day (3x demand that week), snow weeks halve every train's seats, rush weeks multiply demand. MOVES: new line, extend a line end, close a loop, add carriage, interchange upgrade, pick the weekly card, undo this week's edits, run the week. PLANNING AIDS: while planning, every ring shows its FORECAST (how full it gets by the last week if the network stays as drawn) and the HUD shows projected deliveries vs the goal, so a week-1 plan that fails in week 6 is visible in week 1; a lost run restarts from the start of any earlier week.","intent":"BOSS — Meridian Shield. Aha: Two heritage gates, H and K, guard the top corners and send 12 riders a week each. Never put both on one train: give each gate its own short line through its own half of the shield. Run A-H-C-D in the west with the carriage (72 seats) and B-K-F-E in the east (36 seats). Each half's riders stay at home, so the two lines never need to meet. The ring round the whole shield with the carriage (8 hops, 54 seats for 64 riders) carries both gates on one train, and their queues grow every week until both gates fill. Why: Mid-city boss: two heritage stops instead of one. Proof (intended plan, replayed): 384 delivered, goal 269, 3 stars. Trap: one ring round the whole shield with the carriage (8 hops, 54 seats for 64 riders): both gates ride one train and fill by week 4 — loses: H,K full wk4.","mechanics":["carriages","loop lines","heritage stations"],"optimal":7,"branching":8,"trap":0,"explored":2528},{"n":115,"grid":"B-A-P-C-D\n|   ,   |\nF , , , G\nstations: B lantern → 3 moon; A leaf → 3 moon; P moon (HERITAGE) → 1 lantern, 1 drop, 1 key, 1 cup; C star → 3 moon; D key → 3 moon; F drop → 2 moon, 1 leaf; G cup → 2 moon, 1 star\n6 weeks · tracks wk1 +8 · 2 lines · rush wk5 x1.25 · goal 110 of 138 riders · 3rd star: 