ow full it gets by the last week if the network stays as drawn) and the HUD shows projected deliveries vs the goal, so a week-1 plan that fails in week 6 is visible in week 1; a lost run restarts from the start of any earlier week.","intent":"BREATHER — Meridian Gardens. Aha: A quiet afternoon: everyone in the garden rides to or from the heritage fountain P in the middle, so both lines should START there: P-A-B-F west and P-C-D-G east (3 hops, 36 seats each for about 13 riders). The fountain's riders board whichever arm they want and never queue. One line along the whole garden F-B-A-P-C-D-G is 6 hops (18 seats for 26 riders) and falls short. Eight tracks for a six-track answer: the two spare ones forgive a stray first try and are the 3rd star if kept. Why: Breather after the boss: two arms, two lines, six tracks and one clean reading (lines out of the heritage stop), with spare track and a relaxed goal. Proof (intended plan, replayed): 138 delivered, goal 110, 3 stars. Trap: one line along the whole garden F-B-A-P-C-D-G (6 hops, 18 seats for 26 riders) — loses: 70 delivered, goal 110.","mechanics":["rush-hour waves","heritage stations"],"optimal":9,"branching":6,"trap":0,"explored":4536},{"n":116,"grid":"A-B-C\n|   |\nD>E-F\nstations: A leaf → 3 drop, 2 star; B drop → 3 leaf, 2 kite; C star → 3 moon, 2 leaf; D kite (HERITAGE) → 4 leaf, 2 star; E moon → 3 drop, 2 kite; F leaf → 3 star, 2 moon\n7 weeks · tracks wk1 +6 · 1 line · loops allowed · goal 174 of 217 riders · 3rd star: finish with a loop line","legend":"MAP: capital letters = stations (glyph + weekly demand listed under the map); - | \\ / x = rail corridors a line may use (x = two diagonals crossing). TRACKS vs HOPS: one corridor between two stations costs ONE track however long it is drawn ('A---B' is 1 track), but its HOPS are its length in station spacings ('A-B' 1 hop, 'A---B' 2 hops) and each h on it adds 1 more hop; a line's hops set its seats. ~ = river crossing (needs a tunnel); h = hill (each h add